# Rust
backend/target/
backend/.env

# Cargo.lock and backend/.sqlx/ are deliberately NOT ignored. This is an
# application, not a library: the lockfile is what makes a build reproducible,
# so everyone and CI compile the same dependency versions. And `.sqlx/` exists
# precisely so a build can happen without a database to check queries against —
# ignoring it would defeat the one thing it is for. `frontend/package-lock.json`
# has always been committed, and this keeps the two sides consistent.

# Node
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local

